{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts","id":1323141,"title":"What is stopping your Circle from Creating their own Exalts?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-07-09T01:06:51-07:00","id":1323141,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> What is stopping your Circle from Creating their own Exalts?","content":"So whats stopping a Circle, by this I mean specifically the Player Circle, from creating their own Exalted? Be it One off Exalts or even a Batch like Rakan Thulio did, that's the big catch with Exalted the PCs are supposed to have the agency to achieve the greatest of Goals, they even gave systems in the past to replace the Incarna or Primordials. So why not make your own Exalts? Its got to be easier for a group dedicated to a unified purpose compared to a rogue elder. So Five Exalts of varied capabilities, over time they even create Spirit servants and bind Demons and Elementals. Eventually you create an N/A Artifact and some Solar Circle Workings.<br /> <br /> Hells I'd imagine there could be some Exalts from the 1st Age who were Created by the Lords of Creation, or even Secret Exalted Created by Exalted in the Heat of the Primordial War!<br /> <br /> I mean besides the Meta issue of making your own mechanics and charms it feels like a fun goal to have, and its the type of goal that once you achieve it helps you achieve other goals. And if someone Dies you can even have them Play one the Circles own Exalted Creations.<br /> <br /> Any Ideas? I can imagine using even the soul of a deceased Circle Member could be a good Prima Materia. Or even say unifying that soul, with all the past souls who played host to the Exaltation.<br /> <br /> What are some ideas for Projects of this nature? How high would you put your goals? Start with one offs, or make self replicating ones like Dragonblooded, or even creating the Exaltation wholesale like Alchemicals? Lots of cool idea. You could uplift an animal into a humanoid Exalted! The Uplifted Exalted could be fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T01:40:47-07:00","id":1323146,"title":"","content":"Well, for one thing Thulio didn't create the Getimians, he found their Exaltations. Their actual creator(s) are currently unknown.<br /> <br /> Per what Vance has said in Ask the Devs, creating Exalted requires a certain singular and numinous nature; the Incarnae, the Primordials, the 'dark mother', the Wyld entity that creates the Dream-Souled, they all have that nature. So, can the Exalted attain that nature? And if so, how?<br /> <br /> Then there's the matter of the Law of Diminishment; creating Exalted has a permanent cost, and you will be lessened afterwards. Creating Exalted is not done casually or on a whim. There was a reason to do this: what was it? What demanded the creation of new Exalted? What was worth the price?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":51,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","user":"marin","date":". 07-09-2019, 04:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T01:56:34-07:00","id":1323149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323146#post1323146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, for one thing Thulio didn't create the Getimians, he found their Exaltations. Their actual creator(s) are currently unknown.<br /> <br /> Per what Vance has said in Ask the Devs, creating Exalted requires a certain singular and numinous nature; the Incarnae, the Primordials, the 'dark mother', the Wyld entity that creates the Dream-Souled, they all have that nature. So, can the Exalted attain that nature? And if so, how?<br /> <br /> Then there's the matter of the Law of Diminishment; creating Exalted has a permanent cost, and you will be lessened afterwards. Creating Exalted is not done casually or on a whim. There was a role reason to do this: what was it? What demanded the creation of new Exalted? What was worth the price?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I also take it they need to just incorporate the singular Numinous nature, IE discover such a being/a way to apply it to help you. Like discovering a Shinma Platonic Ideal of Heroism, or Immortality, or Villainy. Exigents seem to work like that, where Sol Incarnate fashioned the Divine Flame and the individual gods empower them.<br /> <br /> And yes the Law of Diminishment is my favorite part! What I ponder is how to apply it, maybe if you make one Exalt who can die and vanish then it maybe weakens you like an Odinsleep situation or a permanent Exalt cripples the Exalted who made them, or if you create a new type and a Batch of them you even cripple your Exaltation, I know its a holy cow but I am fine with concepts like shattering an Exaltation. And maybe you can spread the Law of Diminishment with everyone involved so the whole Circle and their Familiar Pantheon are Crippled, after all to make Exigents the Sun was Diminished and the Gods who use it to Exalt are Diminished. Maybe they can do a similar two stage diminishment where they are diminished in creating the potential Exalts and then the Exalting/Manifesting of them Diminishes whoever is involved in this second stage.<br /> <br /> And if they really need to they can create a Singular Numinous being, I always loved the Idea of Exalted Making Baby Primordials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T02:31:32-07:00","id":1323152,"title":"","content":"I loath the Law of Diminishment. Oddly for the exact opposite reason I dislike most of the rest of 3E's take on Exaltation: it's too material and scientific. It's trying to answer 'why didn't they just make infinite exalts?' logically, rather than just allow the act of Exaltation to be inherently mythic, and thus requiring great mythic deeds. All you need to say is 'making more Exalted would be really frecking tough' and you're pretty much golden. The Incarna could try and make more Chosen, but it'd be tough (doubly so without Autochthon), no guarantee it'd work even for them and why bother when they each have their current chosen host?<br /> <br /> By that same token, I don't have an inherent problem with PCs trying to make their own Exaltations, though with the game as it stands I kind of do? It's the principle of The First Age Was a Different Genre; this is the sort of crazy epic thing that IMO should be in the playspace of E6-10 charms. And not only do we not have that, we don't have an easy way to build up to that with the system as it stands. If you're okay with saying that an E5 Solar should be on the same playing field as the greatest of the gods, then I guess just 'N/A project' is fine. It doesn't really break anything: by that point you're already making powerful creatures and servents. You can summon 3rd circle demons, make critters via sorcerous workings, build the Five Metal Shrike or a Thousand Forged Dragon. An Exaltation isn't that much of a step up in power terms, more in thematics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T02:44:40-07:00","id":1323154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323152#post1323152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's trying to answer 'why didn't they just make infinite exalts?' logically...</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, not really.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T03:00:50-07:00","id":1323155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323154#post1323154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, not really.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you've got an alternate rationale, Count, I'd love to hear it. It's how it always read to me, and I dislike it on those grounds. Exaltation should be transcendent, great and miraculous. The LoD makes it feel more like a straight power up 'These guys took some of their power and gave it to you'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T03:10:13-07:00","id":1323156,"title":"","content":"Elohim asking Abraham to sacrifice his son was always my favourite account of a scientific development.<br /> <br /> Xipe Totec flaying his skin to bestow food upon humanity, periodically repaid by offering the removed skins of captives, less so; twas always a bit too corny for my tastes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T03:12:40-07:00","id":1323157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323155#post1323155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you've got an alternate rationale, Count, I'd love to hear it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure.<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Not every introduction of a detail is intended to answer a question.</b><br /> <br /> \u200bI ate ramen noodles twenty hours ago, and a fried egg four hours ago; did I suspect you were the least bit curious about my diet prior to saying that? Of course not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323155#post1323155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's how it always read to me...</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, but consider that maybe sometimes, a cigar is just a cigar?<br /> <br /> <b>Back on topic...</b><br /> <br /> \u200bTo answer the OP, the reason I've never been part of a Circle that made Exalts is twofold.<br /> <br /> One, the thought never occurred to them.<br /> <br /> \u200bTwo, if it <i>did</i>, they'd probably come to the conclusion that creating autonomous free-willed powerful beings and expecting them to do things for you, has a bit of a bad track record, across Creation's history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-09-2019, 06:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T04:21:13-07:00","id":1323164,"title":"","content":"On the subject of the thread, it has been stated by the devs that the creation of Exaltation is something not easily achieved- and by not easily, I mean almost practically impossible. Currently, the only entities to manage to preform the miracle are the Incarnae, a Primordial, the Five Elemental Dragons, the Dark Mother, the Wyld thing which created the Dream-Souled and a Voice in a Trench (as well as whatever the patron of the Getimians may be). Even the Abyssals and the Infernals are basically corrupted forms of existing Exaltation, instead of newly formed ones birthed by their patrons directly.<br /> <br /> Now, the power gap between those entities and practically anything else is enormous- even demons of the Third Circle, the high gods of Heaven, Lesser Elemental Dragons and the Deathlords couldn't produce an Exaltation by their own right. The whole reason that Exigence exists is to allow for gods such as Ahlat, which is among the stronger gods of creation, to create Chosen for themselves without a utter self destruction <i>and still failing in the mission</i>. Corrupting an existing Exaltation seems to require less raw power, but it still requires something more than average to preform the act.<br /> <br /> So in short, while not outright impossible (it is Exalted, after all), cultivating spirits to reach the point they could create Exalts of their own, or forcing a patron of Incarnae-level power to do so against their will (note that finding one such entity in the first place would be the main issue, as such entities don't grow on trees after all and are quit rare) is far from an easy feat, not to mention that, as mention above, those Exalts would not be forced to obey you usually. That would be a material for an whole adventure, which has many places where it could go horribly wrong and many much better alternatives.<br /> <br /> As for the Law of Diminishment, I must say that while I do like the concept, I do have certain troubles with the name. I mean, just stating that the act of creating an Exaltation requires a great cost to preform which could not be easily recovered, if at all, does feel &quot;mythic&quot; to me. But calling it &quot;the Law of Diminishment&quot; turns it from an heroic act from the god's part into &quot;just a mechanism by which nature works&quot;. Kinda like how Coulomb's Law turns the miracle of lightning into just a product of electrons discharging through a medium.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T04:26:01-07:00","id":1323168,"title":"","content":"Currently creating exaltations seems strictly &quot;a thing that doesn't really happen&quot;, and I'd like to keep it that way.<br /> <br /> Be ready for your players to basically turn themselves into unplayable entities and/or cause a small apocalypse in the process, for nothing less would be able to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T04:35:17-07:00","id":1323169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts#post1323141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it feels like a fun goal to have</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it? What kind of gameplay does it entail?<br /> <br /> I mean, okay, fine, I get that it's you asking us, but well, I certainly can't think of an answer. It seems very naval gazing rather than something that can be organically incorporated into play and the kind of storyline progression that seems most suited to a tabletop game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">But calling it &quot;the Law of Diminishment&quot; turns it from an heroic act from the god's part into &quot;just a mechanism by which nature works&quot;.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> How does this square with the fact that the term &quot;law&quot; and its equivalents in various other languages were things first applied to concepts of human relations and religious proscriptions?<br /> <br /> Setting aside any specific religious beliefs, is the Law of Moses a mechanism of nature?<br /> <br /> </span></span></span></div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Kinda like how Coulomb's Law turns the miracle of lightning into just a product of electrons discharging through a medium.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Hmm, I'm pretty sure that's what lightning was before... life existed.<br /> <br /> Coulomb was trying to describe a phenomenon that actually exists, not compose an artistic narrative. </span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T05:11:02-07:00","id":1323171,"title":"","content":"Succeeding in Creating/Discovering a new Exalt sounds like the opposite of naval gazing to me. It can be a whole chronicle in and of itself, incorporating everything from tracking down an unknown Primordial and learning from them, and plumbing the depth of Creation's mysteries, dissecting Exaltations using Lytek's Panoply or reading Jupiter's secret Journal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T05:19:23-07:00","id":1323174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323168#post1323168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Currently creating exaltations seems strictly &quot;a thing that doesn't really happen&quot;, and I'd like to keep it that way.<br /> <br /> Be ready for your players to basically turn themselves into unplayable entities and/or cause a small apocalypse in the process, for nothing less would be able to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean having a Circle go against the Empress in her prime seems to be a thing that doesn't happen but I think that would be a keen thing I would like to tell the story of as well.<br /> <br /> And either Creating your Own Exalted is a culminating point to capstone a Chronicle and becoming something Gnarly, or its not and its a late game point where you involve yourself in something grander then any one member of the Circle. If you are creative you don't need to be so cooky cutter as Become the Sun or a Primordial to Create an Exalt. All the new Exalts are a mystery, involve yourself in a new mystery. You don't need to be as purely paint by numbers as proscribed in the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T05:21:29-07:00","id":1323175,"title":"","content":"Because my players are far more concerned with the personal stories and ambitions of their characters, and their so their characters reflect these goals and drives.<br /> <br /> The Exalted exist for an interesting reason, sure, but this reason is out there partly because we need a reason for the the folks we're playing to exist.<br /> <br /> Maybe you or your players feel like they absolutely want to spend their time mucking about in the metaphysical nuts and bolts of the setting, but to me this whole premise seems contrary to telling an interesting, human story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T05:41:54-07:00","id":1323178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janissary87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323175#post1323175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because my players are far more concerned with the personal stories and ambitions of their characters, and their so their characters reflect these goals and drives.<br /> <br /> The Exalted exist for an interesting reason, sure, but this reason is out there partly because we need a reason for the the folks we're playing to exist.<br /> <br /> Maybe you or your players feel like they absolutely want to spend their time mucking about in the metaphysical nuts and bolts of the setting, but to me this whole premise seems contrary to telling an interesting, human story.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> See now isn't this the type of Patronizing comment some people would get punished for? This is a very poorly veiled slight but I'll bet there will be no consequence for it and it won't be acknowledged as an attempt to goad a reaction. Yet I'll point it out.<br /> <br /> You can make a chronicle about anything, and Creating your own Exalted clearly would not be only that, Every chronicle has more then one thing going on. A modern Prometheus wasn't just about creating life, Victor had Friends and loved ones like Henry Cleval and Elizabeth. Its insincere to suggest these things wouldn't exist just because you are achieving a goal. Do friends, loved ones, relationships, curse and what not not exist if your characters are warring against the Realm, or Finding Zen Mu, or Rest in Peacing a Deathlord?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T05:51:39-07:00","id":1323179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323169#post1323169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> How does this square with the fact that the term &quot;law&quot; and its equivalents in various other languages were things first applied to concepts of human relations and religious proscriptions?<br /> <br /> Setting aside any specific religious beliefs, is the Law of Moses a mechanism of nature?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is a matter of connotation. The Law of Moses actually means a set of laws/ teachings. The Law of Diminishment speaks about a law of nature. Formulating laws of nature is what science do. As such, the Law of Diminishment gains a scientific aesthetics and lose a mythical one, IMO. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hmm, I'm pretty sure that's what lightning was before... life existed.<br /> <br /> Coulomb was trying to describe a phenomenon that actually exists, not compose an artistic narrative. [/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR][/LEFT] </div> </div> </div>Yes, but it is not what people <i>believed</i><i>. </i>They thought it was the will of the gods, or a sign, or some primordial power. Until one day, people understood what lightning really was, and then made a set of equations which explains how and why it worked, and it turned from a mythical entity into an natural phenomenon. <br /> <br /> It is all about presentation, in the end, and by giving a name to a natural phenomenon and formulating it into a law of nature the presentation turns from mythical into scientific, because, in essence, <i>that's what science do</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T05:55:51-07:00","id":1323180,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">See now isn't this the type of Patronizing comment some people would get punished for?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you think they're breaking a rule, report it. Personally I don't see anything <i>resembling </i>a personal attack here, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-09-2019, 09:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T06:00:14-07:00","id":1323181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323174#post1323174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All the new Exalts are a mystery, involve yourself in a new mystery. You don't need to be as purely paint by numbers as proscribed in the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course.<br /> <br /> It's just...ugh, I really don't like it. The deed involves answering questions most of us agreed answering in previous editions was a bad idea. It left a sore wound. I'm not sure you'll get useful intel here.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, to answer the title question: I prefer that subject to remain a creation myth rather than anything tangible.<br /> You may get more useful answers by hitting off your own ideas and fish for the responses that resonate. People will get creative in time if it sticks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 07-09-2019, 09:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T06:05:59-07:00","id":1323182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323180#post1323180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you think they're breaking a rule, report it. Personally I don't see anything resembling a personal attack here, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pointing out how arguments and threadcrapping start here on the Exalted Forums. And I've told you before I don't report people for trifling things, but I sense we never shared such sensibilities. So please continue to hijack about pedantic minutia, just to see who is &quot;right&quot; on opinions and trivial matter.<br /> <br /> I like the Law of Diminishment but others are well in their right to disfavor its addition into Exalted canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T06:07:34-07:00","id":1323183,"title":"","content":"Kind of an unstated premise of the OP is that lots of power eventually equates to some form of omnipotence. That since you should be able to surpass powerful beings in some aspects (mostly in order to defeat them or notably impactful changes to the world) that you should be able to also to do everything they can do but better.<br /> <br /> I think folks get in their head that because the creators were defeated and defeatable, that they have nothing they can do that's off limits to Exalts wihtout downplaying htem. But I Think i'ts just fine to say &quot;Exalts are mighty...they just don't get a blank check.&quot; Exalts can't Exalt because well, they just can't. They are powerful beings, but unless you do something that's basically a &quot;Your story and campaign probably resolves around doing this the first time as its culmination&quot; sort of effort, the assumpion by default probably is it's impossible because Exalted power just doesn't expresss itself in a way to allow it.<br /> <br /> This kind of goes why I don't think we need a Law of Diminishment of late, myself. It could just be the Sun only made around 300 Solars has nothing at all to do with his decisions to do so, or some pain on him in doing so. It might just be that...that's literally the only way he could have made them. &quot;But what if it were different?&quot; is kind of irrelevant. It isn't, and assuming it coudl be has a bit of a begging the question aspect to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T06:09:42-07:00","id":1323184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323181#post1323181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course.<br /> <br /> It's just...ugh, I really don't like it. The deed involves answering questions most of us agreed answering in previous editions was a bad idea. It left a sore wound. I'm not sure you'll get useful intel here.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, to answer the title question: I prefer that subject to remain a creation myth rather than anything tangible.<br /> You may get more useful answers by hitting off your own ideas and fish for the responses that resonate. People will get creative in time if it sticks.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> See I'm fine with that, because in some games I would allow things that in other games I would ban. Its like playing a game were say you do a what if the Solar Exalted were completely destroyed instead of sealed in the Jade Prison. Each game is different and can operate under different assumptions. I've seen several people state they have no intention of including any of the New Exalted introduced in 3rd ed, and that's fine. I can see myself playing in such a game just as I can see myself playing in a mixed new Exalt game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T06:15:02-07:00","id":1323186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323183#post1323183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kind of an unstated premise of the OP is that lots of power eventually equates to some form of omnipotence. That since you should be able to surpass powerful beings in some aspects (mostly in order to defeat them or notably impactful changes to the world) that you should be able to also to do everything they can do but better.<br /> <br /> I think folks get in their head that because the creators were defeated and defeatable, that they have nothing they can do that's off limits to Exalts wihtout downplaying htem. But I Think i'ts just fine to say &quot;Exalts are mighty...they just don't get a blank check.&quot; Exalts can't Exalt because well, they just can't. They are powerful beings, but unless you do something that's basically a &quot;Your story and campaign probably resolves around doing this the first time as its culmination&quot; sort of effort, the assumpion by default probably is it's impossible because Exalted power just doesn't expresss itself in a way to allow it.<br /> <br /> This kind of goes why I don't think we need a Law of Diminishment of late, myself. It could just be the Sun only made around 300 Solars has nothing at all to do with his decisions to do so, or some pain on him in doing so. It might just be that...that's literally the only way he could have made them. &quot;But what if it were different?&quot; is kind of irrelevant. It isn't, and assuming it coudl be has a bit of a begging the question aspect to it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well I don't believe the Exalted can do anything and everything better then the Incarna and Primordials, I didn't state a single player making 300 Perfect Supermen. I had a lot of reservations about even Soloing 3rd Circle souls in a fair fight.<br /> <br /> And I don't see why the Law of Diminishment is an issue... we don't have any specifics besides if you want to make something as potent as an Exalt then it will weaken you in some way. We don't really have the mystical calculus of it, its a pretty freeform rule. Ignore it if you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T06:25:03-07:00","id":1323187,"title":"","content":"Kind of another thing too with why I don't think Exalted shoudl be making sub-Exalts: The game is about you going out into the world and doing shit. While creating other Exlats is doing something, it in the end has this feel of just sub-delegating. Rather than making people able to do more things for you, I think the idea is you should just do things. What does even making an Exaltation like, <i>do</i> for an Exalt besides act as a &quot;Look what I did!&quot; moment. And while there are plenty of things that are that in actions of hubris and glory, it's not really as interesting to me. You don't really <i>do</i> anything with an Exaltaiton save delegate to others. It's an interesting thing for NPCs like the gods because well, they're not supposed to be major actors in the setting. But it's not so clear for an Exalt, because well....Exalts are the ones supposed to be actors doing things besides making more people meant to do things. It's wierdly just kind of recursive to me.<br /> <br /> This also happens especially when themes get involved. Like, what's the Exalted ofa Solar Exalted like? Just an even-more-er filtered version of the Sun? The Sun but filtered through Bob? This is a big issue there too. Unless you have in your mind a clear idea of what the Exalt like....<i>is</i>, then there's not much to be gained from it. It won't be a new Solar since that in the end just kind of feels like the whole &quot;power = blank check&quot; and more makes you an Exaltation Bootlegger than anything interesting. If it is something more distilled to you, I tink that while a cahracter has themes, the kind of limited nature of them (and not being able to back-fill like NPCs can) are probably going ot lead to a weaker Exalt theamtically. A big advice the deves have given on Exigents so far is don't just htink of them as a power gimic, think of the god they're based on and its thematics. Gods have a bonus of being able to have weird mish-mash of thematics. And Exalted are reflective of their patrons, so that's good to have. I fail to kind of see what a Solar gives in that regard that's not just....more Solar. If the goal ils just blank &quot;Exaltation!&quot; then there's already an issue since Exaltation manifests in diverse ways based on patron. While a Chosen of an Exalt is likely going to be very much like the Exalt, whcih is very muc hlike th patron, which then isn't actually as interesting besies existing in itself.<br /> <br /> Note in this context, finding is different than creating. Rakan released the Getimians, he doesn't have really any control on them. His relationship is one of a mentor and a patron it seems like, not some controller/creator. This isn't actually a bad area for PCs, but again, probably is rare enough to not just be something you assume due to &quot;My Circle is powerful enough.&quot; Getimians have their own things, idea,s and concepts beyond their relation to Rakan Thulio. He imparts their reason to be in the setting, but none of their powers, themes, and such. They're pretty expliclty not his Chosen. Because their patron, whatever the hell it was, is probably very much designed and written in its own way expansive enough to support an Exalt, that a single powerful-but-pissed-off Chosen of Endings probably doesn't do so well for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T06:50:00-07:00","id":1323189,"title":"","content":"Blaque has hit a lot of the points I would. I feel like the difference in metaphysical nature between the patron and their Exalted is significant, a tacit admission that the god or whatever is unable to act, either by some sort of restriction, or by a sort of narrative law that this is the place of a hero and not an inhuman power.<br /> <br /> Exalted creating Exalted of their own just feels like hubris to me in that light.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T16:03:57-07:00","id":1323301,"title":"","content":"The problem with PCs making Exalts is that unless you're reducing them to a commodity, the most natural thing to do is to shift the story focus onto them. This is true of Dragon-Blooded who start their own households and Alchemicals who become cities, designing your own Exalt type with their own charmset really doubles down on this IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T16:49:46-07:00","id":1323312,"title":"","content":"The creation of exalted is a means, not an end. It is done when there is something the entity wishes to do that they cannot do themselves.<br /> <br /> So, far from something that becomes inevitable with omnipotence, the creation of exalted hinges on a lack of power in some regard. An omnipotent being would have no cause to exalt anyone at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T18:14:11-07:00","id":1323329,"title":"","content":"Also, wouldn't it just be easier to gain pressure or leverage over a spirit with exigence to get them to create an exalt for you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T20:08:16-07:00","id":1323348,"title":"","content":"I am not sure how I feel about my players in particular creating exalts but I have toyed with enemy groups in the past having their own \u2018versions\u2019 of exaltation. I haven\u2019t used any of them but I like the idea of \u2018human made\u2019 champions.<br /> <br /> The simplest one was an infernal cult that learned a theurgic ritual to summons demons into a person creating a persona/stand like power set. They would be weaker than dragon-blooded but could also move undetected among the peasantry.<br /> <br /> Another that I might expand upon when exigents comes out is based on ancient Egypt. Basically a special ghost poses a willing and worthy person becoming one with them. The \u2018exalts\u2019 would be very tied to place as they would need to rest in their tombs to recharge their energies. They were going to be a rival kingdom to Persaud that the players could either convince to be allies or antagonize. I really like the idea I had for them because they are human made exaltations out of human souls for the purpose of protecting humans (or rather their kingdom) and sustained by human effort. They were going to be both weaker in some areas and strong in others than Dragonblooded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T20:17:04-07:00","id":1323349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323189#post1323189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blaque has hit a lot of the points I would. I feel like the difference in metaphysical nature between the patron and their Exalted is significant, a tacit admission that the god or whatever is unable to act, either by some sort of restriction, or by a sort of narrative law that this is the place of a hero and not an inhuman power.<br /> <br /> Exalted creating Exalted of their own just feels like hubris to me in that light.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh its meant to be Hubris, and like going out in the Wyld to create their own world it backfiring can work for the story too, or at least having unintended consequences.<br /> <br /> But there are a lot of things you can want that by definition you can't do yourself. You can't birth your own Grandson for instance, well you could in a way but lets not.<br /> Or even just empowering your family, not something as simple as sorcery something genuine like creating a familial line of Guardians to ensure their prosperity. Or even ensure your culture survives, as many Exalted have discovered their birthcultures don't survive the test of Apocalypse as a sure thing.<br /> <br /> And you could be busy in another endeavor like war or discovery and say want someone to be a hero for a place you don't want to live, like say Malfeas, the Underworld, Rakshastan, Heaven, the Ocean, the Sky, or Underground.<br /> <br /> And there is the idea you want a legacy that extends beyond your lifetime. If half the Solars have been Compromised into not being Solars anymore and the Exigent's aren't reliably something you always want then you could want legacies that will survive you to fill in the missing spaces in the heroic tableau of creation.<br /> <br /> But two facet question. What is wrong with doing this as a capstone or Epilogue in a game, and what is wrong with doing it in the middle of a game. They should be two different discussions in a lot aspects. We mostly seem to have addressed only the latter. And a lot of good points have been made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T20:19:48-07:00","id":1323351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323348#post1323348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not sure how I feel about my players in particular creating exalts but I have toyed with enemy groups in the past having their own \u2018versions\u2019 of exaltation. I haven\u2019t used any of them but I like the idea of \u2018human made\u2019 champions.<br /> <br /> The simplest one was an infernal cult that learned a theurgic ritual to summons demons into a person creating a persona/stand like power set. They would be weaker than dragon-blooded but could also move undetected among the peasantry.<br /> <br /> Another that I might expand upon when exigents comes out is based on ancient Egypt. Basically a special ghost poses a willing and worthy person becoming one with them. The \u2018exalts\u2019 would be very tied to place as they would need to rest in their tombs to recharge their energies. They were going to be a rival kingdom to Persaud that the players could either convince to be allies or antagonize. I really like the idea I had for them because they are human made exaltations out of human souls for the purpose of protecting humans (or rather their kingdom) and sustained by human effort. They were going to be both weaker in some areas and strong in others than Dragonblooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've contemplated similar things and what would be the best way to go about it. I've played with the idea of Fomori/Ferectoi from Werewolf of Demon Possessed mutants too.<br /> <br /> And I still plan to create a version of Irem in Creation with the 42 Judges, Shan'iatu and Arisen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T20:54:49-07:00","id":1323362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323349#post1323349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh its meant to be Hubris, and like going out in the Wyld to create their own world it backfiring can work for the story too, or at least having unintended consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'm against it in part because creating a world is more interesting than creating an Exalt. To me it kind of makes Exaltation feel like, as said elsewhere, the ends not the means. I don't think anything is added to Exalts by generating more Exalts. I think it actually kind of dilutes it since it makes it just part of a checklist of &quot;Things power Exalts do because they're powerful&quot; rather than something that feels thematically coherent or interesting. It's not just that it's hubris. It's kind of entitlement and htis assumption that Solar Exaltation is omnipotence that I don't like.<br /> <br /> Hell, I'd argue attempts to do it and failing are probably always going to be more itnersting than some assumption that enough Solarness = you get to do this too. But I also think folks over-sold the &quot;Prove the impossible!&quot; bit at times and that buying into this hype that everything can be done ever makes nothing actually feel challenging or narratively significant as constraints. I like things working in narrative boudnaries. I think sub-Exaltation is one that dilutes, rather than helps, and so shouldn't really be on the table. The reason they don't get to do it is simply put, it's just not good narrative that they can in my view.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323349#post1323349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But there are a lot of things you can want that by definition you can't do yourself. You can't birth your own Grandson for instance, well you could in a way but lets not.<br /> Or even just empowering your family, not something as simple as sorcery something genuine like creating a familial line of Guardians to ensure their prosperity. Or even ensure your culture survives, as many Exalted have discovered their birthcultures don't survive the test of Apocalypse as a sure thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do those need to be Chosen? Lunars seem to get by making beastfolk without having them be Exalted. The Empress has her Legion of Silence. And Volivat has its Ten-Fathered folks running about. There are other ways to do this that probably just are going to be as useful and diverse rather than boiling it down to &quot;A bootleg Exaltation will solve my issues!&quot; None of this need be Exalted. And I think that saying they have to both undersells the effort of Exaltation and cheapens what it was origianlly you know, for. The Sun did it to shake the world order and overthrow the creators. Not to have someone deal with his immortal trust fund.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323349#post1323349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you could be busy in another endeavor like war or discovery and say want someone to be a hero for a place you don't want to live, like say Malfeas, the Underworld, Rakshastan, Heaven, the Ocean, the Sky, or Underground.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you want Secretary Exalted? This doesn't actually, to me, help your case. A Chosen can't be everywhere at once. She should build a network of allies, and compatriots of diverse sorts to help where she can't be. Exaltation, especially in 3e, isn't meant to just be a power pellet. But I gather here it's basically you want to have Chosen fo Doing My Shit For Me, which isn't a strong case. And again, doesn't really get into what the Exaltation is besides &quot;Something useful for the Exalt.&quot; It's theamtically hollow and wasteful in a world where there's hundreds of other ways to empower people that can fill those roles without having to be Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323349#post1323349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And there is the idea you want a legacy that extends beyond your lifetime. If half the Solars have been Compromised into not being Solars anymore and the Exigent's aren't reliably something you always want then you could want legacies that will survive you to fill in the missing spaces in the heroic tableau of creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>This goes a bit into my bit of &quot;Working in constraints is better than just giving folks the whole palette&quot;. Deal with what you have and make that work, don't try to go around making knock-offs like that is somehow the Solution. And that you don't get your legacy to last forever, that eventually you too can be Ozymandius, is something I'm fine saying you can try to fix. But again, nothing of it requires an Exaltation. Non-Exalted stuff can't probably stand the task, but there's always an Ending remember. Even your legacy will fail.<br /> <br /> More Exalts does nothing to fix or fill this. It just turns Exaltation eventually something cheap. &quot;Oh this area needs a new Exalt, better pop one out. Utopia forever!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323349#post1323349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But two facet question. What is wrong with doing this as a capstone or Epilogue in a game, and what is wrong with doing it in the middle of a game. They should be two different discussions in a lot aspects. We mostly seem to have addressed only the latter. And a lot of good points have been made.</div> </div> </div> </div>Capstone I could care less, but I think that you haven't given a compelling reason why it would be interesting an end. Mostly since the &quot;Exalted of an Exalt&quot; sounds like, to not mince words, one of the least tangible and sensible things. What you describe to me sounds like Secretary Exalted, not something worthy of the title. If their whole point is just extend a Solar Exalt's presence and ability to be omnipotent, I don't really think I would like it since I don't like a &quot;And they lived happily ever after.&quot; The goals you note that htey would be there to prevent, I think shouldn't be goals osmeone should reasonably ever feel are ever perfectly achieveable. The only thing you can be sure in time is there's always an Ending. Even to your legacy.<br /> <br /> As for mid-game, the big one is that unless you are taking the time to build-out an entire new Exalt type with Charms, themes and such, that is more than window dressing for characters to show How Cool They Are, then it doesn't to me add much in-game, distracts and wastes times if anything, and cheapens/dilutes Exaltation themes since youb asically are turning them into something your character gets to succeed at making and pat themselvs on the back, rather than you know,a ctually use their power to do things instead of delegating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T21:17:41-07:00","id":1323367,"title":"","content":"One thing I forgot to correct, these aren't supposed to be twice removed Sun Exalted, these aren't supposed to be watered down versions of Solars. The idea is they make something different.<br /> <br /> And I don't know why you would assume Secretary when I list being active in another world you will not travel to. You refuse to move to the Underworld because you can't effectively serve on that front and your busy debating Immaculates so you make something that can and is inclined to exist there. And Doing your stuff for you is one way of putting it, another way is trying to solve problems that aren't your personal problems.<br /> <br /> I mean I'm also getting the impression from this we don't need Exalted period from your opinion because why not just use Beastmen and Gods. And how are Beastmen and Tenparented beings not even more watered down Exalted?<br /> <br /> Most games I am probably not going to tackle this issue of making Exalted, but I don't see it as a particular holy cow on the small scale. Basically its okay if you reveal new Exalted, but you can't have players or even Antagonists involved in the creation of Exalted?<br /> <br /> And the Creation of a single Exalted, some that you could replicate with just Exigents if you were so inclined, is an absolute nono? Being a creator and knowledge seeker is a common goal, like for Twilights and Zeniths for instance. And even if you say couldn't make an Exalt, I don't see why it would be an invalid goal. Like even things that are solidly impossible in the game like Timetravel and Resurrection are still valid goals for characters to strive for, even if you have no intention of making it possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T00:07:19-07:00","id":1323386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323301#post1323301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with PCs making Exalts is that unless you're reducing them to a commodity, the most natural thing to do is to shift the story focus onto them. This is true of Dragon-Blooded who start their own households and Alchemicals who become cities, designing your own Exalt type with their own charmset really doubles down on this IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, while I can imagine playing an Exalt who wants to create a new type of Exalted, it feels like that success in the endeavor would mark the end of that character's story as a PC. She has cemented her legend as a human who ascended to be on par with the Incarnae and forever transformed the world. Continuing play would seem to me to require anticlimax, tragedy, or both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T03:50:59-07:00","id":1323409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323386#post1323386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed, while I can imagine playing an Exalt who wants to create a new type of Exalted, it feels like that success in the endeavor would mark the end of that character's story as a PC. She has cemented her legend as a human who ascended to be on par with the Incarnae and forever transformed the world. Continuing play would seem to me to require anticlimax, tragedy, or both.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have to end the game sometime, and it could work to just switch play to the new character. Like playing a game where you create a might God and that Divine Familiar creates its own Exigent and you switching to it.<br /> <br /> But again I don't believe its 100% to have it be the end of play. and I believe there are ways of achieving it without becoming akin to an Incarna yourself. You could essentially just be discovering a new being that is on the level of Autochthon or a Shinma and work in conjunction with it to create the new Exalted.<br /> <br /> Or what if you go to a Primordial or a Yozis and try to work with one of them to Create an Exalted. You could help them like Auto Helped the Sun.<br /> <br /> Its hardly you won the game and there are so many things to do in Creation. Or perhaps the process of Creating the Exalted Requires you to enter a 1000 year slumber as part of the Law of Diminishment, or even just a hundred years, it would certainly be interesting to do a time skip.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T07:22:12-07:00","id":1323439,"title":"","content":"I think the Yennin are the sort of thing you get when solars or the like try to create a race of empowered humans. Not exalted, but approaching that level of power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T14:19:45-07:00","id":1323520,"title":"","content":"I think my reaction to a player wanting to do this would revolve a lot around the concept, proposed power level, and how it reproduces (is there a set number? How many?).<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the Yennin are the sort of thing you get when solars or the like try to create a race of empowered humans. Not exalted, but approaching that level of power. </div> </div> </div>I'd agree with that. I wouldn't really want PCs to create a bunch of exalts as powerful as them, because I think it'd be deprotagonising. But it depends on the part of the game; at the end of the game, I don't really mind how canon-breaking are.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T19:14:45-07:00","id":1323579,"title":"","content":"<br /> What are Yennin?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323520#post1323520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think my reaction to a player wanting to do this would revolve a lot around the concept, proposed power level, and how it reproduces (is there a set number? How many?).<br /> <br /> Generally speaking,<br /> I'd agree with that. I wouldn't really want PCs to create a bunch of exalts as powerful as them, because I think it'd be deprotagonising. But it depends on the part of the game; at the end of the game, I don't really mind how canon-breaking are.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Dragonblooded do it all the time though... And you can still do it by having Exigents you influenced into being Exalted. But I don't figure they would be Solar level, but Celestial at best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T21:07:02-07:00","id":1323602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323579#post1323579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are Yennin?</div> </div> </div> </div>The people from Volivat who through a First Age relic are able to have eleven parents and as a result have superhuman capabilities. Also called the Ten-Fathered.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323579#post1323579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragonblooded do it all the time though... And you can still do it by having Exigents you influenced into being Exalted. But I don't figure they would be Solar level, but Celestial at best.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon-Blooded Exaltation perpetuates itself through the Terrestrial bloodline. DBs no more &quot;make&quot; more Exalts their power level than a Solar Exalt makes her successor. It's a part of the process, and notably, narrative themes of the Dragon-Blooded to be able to be part of a dynasty of demigods. Solar Exaltation doesn't beget more Solar Exaltations since it was decided early on that Solar Exalted <i>don't</i> make more Exalts, because your legacy being just that, your legacy, is resonant with different htings.<br /> <br /> Note I call your idea Secretary Exalts in part because you have yet to give me themes or ideas to them besides pure utilitarian &quot;These fill in where you can't.&quot; A big push-back I have and others I think express, is that what you want is a servant race to call Exalts of your own and feel good about doing that to Exaltation. A big thing with the game, especially 3e, is that the Exaltation is kind of meant to be something a bit more unique/special than something a person who's just happens to be powerful enough to just make their own.<br /> <br /> Note that an Exigent, you have to 1) Have a god willing to do it 2) Have the Sun willing to grant it and 3) Have the guy still willing to do what youw ant after they Exalt. All I see so far is youw anting in effect still &quot;Servant Exalts&quot;. A sort of Chosen who's notable as they can do the underling shit for another Chosen, something Exalted 3e especially is just plain getting away from. Exalts are their own people, even in a Dynasty like the Dragon-Blooded. And any subservience is one out of societal origins, not because you created their power and expect them to do your shit for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T21:50:40-07:00","id":1323609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323579#post1323579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragonblooded do it all the time though... And you can still do it by having Exigents you influenced into being Exalted. But I don't figure they would be Solar level, but Celestial at best.</div> </div> </div> </div>Celestial at best...<br /> You are aware you just said &quot;I don't expect them to be top tier, but I still expect them to be top tier.&quot; But yeah as Blaque has said your examples don't work, since Dragonblood exaltation was designed with the prospect of inherited power and that the best control they have over making more of DBs is waiting 10-20 years before having another kid and hoping for the best. Which isn't really what you're going for. Your Exigent idea is also going at it from the wrong since it doesn't matter if you talk some mortal into going for it they have to find a god -or gods- who have been granted Exigence (or possess the means to get it) and then are willing to maim or obliterate themselves to empower this mortal.<br /> <br /> Essentially you've conflated the body creating antibodies with creating a vaccine, and being able to paint your warhammer 40k miniatures with making them from the ground up.<br /> <br /> Now here's the thing with a lot of the arguments you've tried making and basically in answer to your question. A lot of this stuff is fiat, your argument that one doesn't need to become equal to any of the Incarna because you could find an entity on that tier to be your coworker and do any parts of the load that require obscene amounts of power. Then the other part is well it doesn't interest my groups, because its well boring and more work than its worth to do. I mean from the stuff I've seen it tends to come down to go other places I don't want to go and do stuff I don't want to or can't do because I'm busy. None of those strike me as particularly engaging, and trying to make them to handle work you can't doesn't help because you're basically saying &quot;I don't have time to go handle this job because I'm in the middle of a war, so I'm going to divert my attention from the war to create a means of empowering a new recruit and hope that eventually they'll have power on par with my own, or at least enough to do what I want, not that their potential power will matter as they'll be dealing with this job with travel time as the length of time they've been empowered for.&quot;<br /> <br /> Mind I say all this as we seem to ehewing the more traditional route of using a sorcerous working to give a mortal powers and abilities in some fashion even if they might only last for a generation, even though that is technically how most Exigents are just with the caveat that there's likely a dead or maimed god left behind their creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":". 07-11-2019, 12:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T23:52:52-07:00","id":1323622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323157#post1323157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI ate ramen noodles twenty hours ago, and a fried egg four hours ago; did I suspect you were the least bit curious about my diet prior to saying that? Of course not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I <i>wasn't</i>, but now I'm concerned that you're not eating right if that's all you've had in twenty hours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T01:18:18-07:00","id":1323628,"title":"","content":"The things I'm not crazy about in the premises are:<br /> <br /> - Exalted themed off existing Exalted: It doesn't seem like the themes of the personalities of PCs as a particular Solar, etc. lend themselves as much to new Exalted as those of gods. I'm a bit suss of that sort of thing as it seems like the weak themes of the &quot;Devil Tigers&quot;.<br /> - Suggestion (if I detect it right) that Exalted kind of &quot;graduate&quot; at high levels of power to their own Exalted is a bit rote and seems inconsistent with setting history.<br /> <br /> Those said, I wouldn't be against a character whose mission and thing is to be the handmaid of spreading the Exigency or finding new Exalted. Possibly more an NPC sort of thing though.<br /> In terms of totally creating totally new Exalted which are original, with a lot more investment of a character's personal power in doing so, I think you would need to find a strong rationale for why this is something a character would want to do.<br /> <br /> The Unconquered Sun created the Solars to be agents and champions of his will in the world and to fight his enemies, tasks that he was unsuitable to do directly (the Great Geas and the scale and restrictions of his power). The gods seek their own Exigent Exalted (when they do) for the same reasons.<br /> <br /> What is there that your PC can't do that she would want to go to the challenge of creating a new type of champion at huge personal expense of power to do? Exalted have a lot of capabilities already, though any particular Exalted is limited.<br /> <br /> If you can come up with an excellent rationale that works for your story, then I think it could work. But not without that. There's nothing un-thematic in Exalted to the story of a mighty Exalted sorcerer who sacrifices his life or magic to empower a human as a powerful champion of his will, with strange powers that no existing Exalted can exactly replicate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T02:26:49-07:00","id":1323635,"title":"","content":"Exalted is the kind of game where, if the point of something trying to create Chosen is hubris, then the answer should be about what kind of interesting disaster they end up making by accident.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T06:30:34-07:00","id":1323662,"title":"","content":"Isn't this basically the same role that Half-Caste(though I understand that terminology is going away) offspring served in previous editions? With the Breed True trait, they can compensate with quantity over quality(as weird as it is saying that about hypothetical people). Hell, Dreams of the First Age mentioned the Solars founding dynasties of golden-children in Meru.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T07:19:40-07:00","id":1323670,"title":"","content":"Hah, that's true Isator; Liminals are the product of one kind of hubris, this could perhaps be another.<br /> <br /> Essentially, I wouldn't give it a hard no, because I think that there are maybe good stories you can tell. But a)most of them (not all) can be done with sorcerous workings, wtc, rather than creating exalts, b) making exalts of celestial level who are des to serve you, and that's it... isn't one of them.<br /> Actually, my tolerance for it would probably depend a lot in how much control the PC has over them. And, of course, if they have a cool concept for them.<br /> <br /> I guess I put making your own Exalted in the same category as resurrection, the Yozis escaping, or time travel. If there's a good concept for it I'm fine with the ST allowing it, but I understand why people are hesitant, and why the devs generally say that you can't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T07:37:21-07:00","id":1323677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HamSandLich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323662#post1323662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't this basically the same role that [racist slur] offspring served in previous editions?</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, there's a pretty solid difference between empowering someone, and having a child with someone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HamSandLich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323662#post1323662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the Breed True trait...</div> </div> </div> </div>Was that something they could take, though? I'll admit, I haven't looked at the book in years, but I seem to recall it not being compatible with the ability to use Essence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HamSandLich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323662#post1323662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(as weird as it is saying that about hypothetical people)</div> </div> </div> </div>You're telling me! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T07:38:40-07:00","id":1323678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323670#post1323670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hah, that's true Isator; Liminals are the product of one kind of hubris</div> </div> </div> </div>What are you basing that on?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essentially, I wouldn't give it a hard no, because I think that there are maybe good stories you can tell. But a)most of them (not all) can be done with sorcerous workings, wtc, rather than creating exalts, b) making exalts of celestial level who are des to serve you, and that's it... isn't one of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The comparison to workings makes me think about how that's able to be a much more straightforward action in comparison because the consequences of creating Exalted are greater than that of any working.<br /> <br /> In a sense of theme and character, mind, not necessarily saying that they're all the ultimate power.<br /> <br /> But given that weight of consequence, it raises questions about what such a game would actually consist of. It ought not to be something as straightforward and mechanical as a working, because the setting ascribes higher stakes to it.<br /> <br /> And even if it's a procedure that is coherent, is it especially satisfying to play? I think some things should be given a hard no if they amount to story and gameplay cul de sacs.<br /> <br /> On a side note, somebody before mentioned the idea of coercing a god into seeking the Exigence by your specifications. Setting aside the likelihood that in-character any given Chosen of a small god isn't precisely designed, I feel as though any spirit who could be susceptible to such pressure would be weak enough for Diminishment to consume them. That feels like a narrative dramatically inclined towards ending up with an Exalt strongly calibrated to seek vengeance against you for having wronged the god so.<br /> <br /> Certainly, if one considers the Lawgivers to be on probation with the Unconquered Sun, doing that kind of shit around a process in which he has direct attention and involvement is a bad idea. It seems like a fitting story that he'd grant the petition that he knows is truly going on in the god's heart in order to teach the wayward Solar a lesson about hubris.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T08:04:37-07:00","id":1323686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323678#post1323678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What are you basing that on?</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine they're talking about how you create a liminal. IE: a human attempts to resurrect someone or create life from stitched together corpses and the dark mother intervenes to actually make it succeed. <br /> <br /> The liminal is then forever after tied to it's creator until they die.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T08:22:18-07:00","id":1323690,"title":"","content":"The attempt to create life from the dead is the circumstance that enables the Dark Mother to work, but as I recall it no part of the Exaltation comes from anything besides herself, and she's apparently wearing herself down with every Chernozem she makes.<br /> <br /> But sure, at least one of the Liminal Aspects goes to bodies being worked by somebody driven by hubris. Not all, though; there is despair and desperation among them.<br /> <br /> The motives of the one creating the actual Essence seem as though they would have higher aspirations. All that dealing with ghosts and the boundaries of the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T09:47:29-07:00","id":1323708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323677#post1323677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, there's a pretty solid difference between empowering someone, and having a child with someone.<br /> <br /> Was that something they could take, though? I'll admit, I haven't looked at the book in years, but I seem to recall it not being compatible with the ability to use Essence.<br /> <br /> You're telling me! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I apologize if i've offended. Didn't mean to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T09:59:59-07:00","id":1323711,"title":"","content":"My operating theory for some time has been that Exalts really shouldn't be able to create more Exalts, <i>but</i>, they should be able to create something new that is to Exalts as Exalts are to gods or gods are to Primordials or Primordials are to... the... infinite roiling Wyld? So:<br /> <br /> Whatever it was in the Wyld that gave rise to the Primordials, if such things are meaningfully distinct -&gt; Primordials -&gt; Gods -&gt; Exalted -&gt; ????<br /> <br /> Because if the answer to the question &quot;What comes next in the cycle after Exalted?&quot; is &quot;More Exalted, possibly forever,&quot; that's boring.<br /> <br /> (And yes, I know there's arguably another version of this that goes Wyld -&gt; Primordials -&gt; elementals -&gt; Whatever the elementals could have gotten around to doing, if they had, which they don't appear to have done.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T10:26:27-07:00","id":1323718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323711#post1323711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My operating theory for some time has been that Exalts really shouldn't be able to create more Exalts, <i>but</i>, they should be able to create something new that is to Exalts as Exalts are to gods or gods are to Primordials or Primordials are to... the... infinite roiling Wyld? So:<br /> <br /> Whatever it was in the Wyld that gave rise to the Primordials, if such things are meaningfully distinct -&gt; Primordials -&gt; Gods -&gt; Exalted -&gt; ????<br /> <br /> Because if the answer to the question &quot;What comes next in the cycle after Exalted?&quot; is &quot;More Exalted, possibly forever,&quot; that's boring.<br /> <br /> (And yes, I know there's arguably another version of this that goes Wyld -&gt; Primordials -&gt; elementals -&gt; Whatever the elementals could have gotten around to doing, if they had, which they don't appear to have done.)</div> </div> </div> </div>given that draconic forms are a type of enlightment, wouldn't it be elementals-&gt;dragons","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T10:42:41-07:00","id":1323722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323678#post1323678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What are you basing that on?</div> </div> </div> </div>That it's hubris to try and cheat death?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The comparison to workings makes me think about how that's able to be a much more straightforward action in comparison because the consequences of creating Exalted are greater than that of any working.<br /> <br /> In a sense of theme and character, mind, not necessarily saying that they're all the ultimate power. </div> </div> </div>That was partially my point.<br /> <br /> If you want to create magical servants, you can already do it via workings. One of my friends made a whole bunch of western-style dragons; they fly, they breathe fire, etc. He also enchanted most of his (well, her, the character is female) populace to turn them into Mernii, a race of 6'6&quot; pallid magical elf-like people with better stats, some of whom have jet black skin with fiery veins and fire-magic.<br /> Another friend's sorcerer made a dualistic guardian spirit who has two bodies with two forms each; at night a small orbiting moon and also a four-armed warrior woman, and in the day a small orbiting sun and also a snarky tall blue male warrior. He's now working on a set of dragon's teeth that he can throw in a lake to produce a swarm of aggressive gribbly monsters who'll die after a few hours, and a sneaky chameolonic monster spirit that can stalk his enemies in the jungle before jumping out and ripping them apart with its claws.<br /> <br /> If you want to create a powerful servant, or a race of servants, you can already do it in a way that is less awkward for the setting.<br /> And if you want to just empower humanity, you're probably better off making huge numbers of people more resistant to disease and aging (as one of my players did near the end of my 2nd ed game with a Craft: Genesis parasite that empowers its host).<br /> <br /> To create self-replicating power that passes from mortal to mortal (either by inheritance, magic, or sticking their souls into golems) achieves little more than that* for you, but is perhaps more disruptive to the setting, thematically.<br /> <br /> *Unless the point is to create, in the long-term, way more powerful champions. Which I think is an issue in of itself, in terms of deprotagonising the players (already an issue with, say, 2nd circle demons, and I imagine 3rd circles though I've never actually seen any players summon a 3rd circle).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It ought not to be something as straightforward and mechanical as a working, because the setting ascribes higher stakes to it. </div> </div> </div>Definitely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think some things should be given a hard no if they amount to story and gameplay cul de sacs. </div> </div> </div>Indeed. That's why I think I'd be much more okay with this near the end of the game than halfway through.<br /> <br /> (Unfortunately, this has led to issues for my successor. I was much more lenient with the players' schemes, aggressive nation-building and workings near the end of my game, as I was fairly happy to end the game with &quot;you win, well done.&quot; But they wanted to keep playing, and the guy who took over the game found some of this problematic.)<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T10:55:03-07:00","id":1323726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323718#post1323718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">given that draconic forms are a type of enlightment, wouldn't it be elementals-&gt;dragons</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, dragons are a type of elemental, not the children of elementals, so maybe or maybe not. Hard to say. My point in including that parenthetical was &quot;Yes, I'm aware not every element of the setting supports this argument.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T11:14:23-07:00","id":1323729,"title":"","content":"But gods do create other gods and Primordials do create other Primordials though?<br /> <br /> (Agree that if Exalted are creating Exalt as an analogy to the cycle of being Primordials-&gt;gods-&gt;Exalted, then that's not quite right. But it's not so clear to me that's the intent).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T11:43:30-07:00","id":1323734,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s not clear whether Primordials ever created more Primordials. Gods definitely create more gods, though.<br /> <br /> That said, Exalts creating more Exalts so they\u2019ll have Exalts to work for them rather than peers definitely fits the Primordial -&gt; God -&gt; Exalt pattern cycle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T13:02:34-07:00","id":1323755,"title":"","content":"Gods usually create gods in the same manner that some exalts can make more exalts, so I don't think that's an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T13:05:45-07:00","id":1323756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323755#post1323755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gods usually create gods in the same manner that some exalts can make more exalts, so I don't think that's an issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was about to say. Gods don't seem to go out of their way to make more of them, besides uplifting humans to be something in the god's purview, or were their kid. Or well...the old fashioned method gods in methology make more gods. Which is like saying rabbits amke more rabbits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T13:26:14-07:00","id":1323761,"title":"","content":"And Dragonblood make more Dragonblood, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T14:11:20-07:00","id":1323775,"title":"","content":"Yeah, there you go. Gods can make more gods largely via the same way DBs make more DBs. For Exalts without access to that method, attempts to make new Exalts should probably result in \u201cThis doesn\u2019t work, but the method by which it fails suggests promising new avenues of research!\u201d the end result of which is the creation of... something new.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T14:22:15-07:00","id":1323776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323711#post1323711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My operating theory for some time has been that Exalts really shouldn't be able to create more Exalts, <i>but</i>, they should be able to create something new that is to Exalts as Exalts are to gods or gods are to Primordials or Primordials are to... the... infinite roiling Wyld? So:<br /> <br /> Whatever it was in the Wyld that gave rise to the Primordials, if such things are meaningfully distinct -&gt; Primordials -&gt; Gods -&gt; Exalted -&gt; ????<br /> <br /> Because if the answer to the question &quot;What comes next in the cycle after Exalted?&quot; is &quot;More Exalted, possibly forever,&quot; that's boring.<br /> <br /> (And yes, I know there's arguably another version of this that goes Wyld -&gt; Primordials -&gt; elementals -&gt; Whatever the elementals could have gotten around to doing, if they had, which they don't appear to have done.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. I've maintained, whenever this conversation comes up, that you're the champion of a god; to make a champion of a champion is weirdly hubristic in the way that Exalted characters might plausibly attempt in-game, but many folks never seem to realize why it doesn't make a ton of sense out of game. Your power stems from the Unconquered Sun, or from Luna, or the Maidens, or whatever; it isn't wholly <i>yours</i>. Exaltation is a gift, and making a new gift out of the old one doesn't really work.<br /> <br /> Still, at your table, do what you think is fun. If you want to kickstart the next turn of the cycle, go bananas.<br /> <br /> As for the Law of Diminishment, while I doubt we'll ever mention that by name in a book, I think it's an attempt to curb the Infinite Exalts issue of &quot;Why can't my Twilight make Orichalcum Castes? Or their own &lt;Twilight Name Here&gt; Caste?&quot;, which is bizarrely circular and recursive as an endgame goal, and carries a lot of assumptions with it, like &quot;And they'll all do what I say!&quot;, because that has historically worked well in <b>Exalted</b>'s canon. It's also a Tolkien reference in a game deliberately devoid of them, which makes me think it's not a deliberate Tolkien reference: You <i>can</i> make something greater than yourself, but you forever diminish yourself in doing so. Sauron's creation of the Rings forever changes and diminishes him. With the Ring, and those it Chooses, comes great power, but without the Ring Sauron's but a shadow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T14:37:36-07:00","id":1323780,"title":"","content":"I feel the need to point out here that if you <i>really</i> want to \u201cMake new Exalta,\u201d what you really need is a lot of social influence dice, a pliable god, and a catastrophe. There\u2019s nothing stopping you from engineering an emergency worthy of the Exigence and then convincing a god to make an Exigent, and this is categorically similar to doing so via sorcerous working inasmuch as both methods involve equal parts rolling dice and convincing your ST to let you get away with your shenanigans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T15:57:33-07:00","id":1323796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323755#post1323755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gods usually create gods in the same manner that some exalts can make more exalts, so I don't think that's an issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... With respect, where the shinto-Celestial Bureaucracy-myth gods of Exalted make new gods, I'm fairly certain they have a bunch more ways to do it than sex. (Or they should).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T16:23:03-07:00","id":1323801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323796#post1323796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm... With respect, where the shinto-Celestial Bureaucracy-myth gods of Exalted make new gods, I'm fairly certain they have a bunch more ways to do it than sex. (Or they should).</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean sure, but at the same time, it <i>is</i> how a good chunk of them also come about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T16:40:19-07:00","id":1323806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323780#post1323780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel the need to point out here that if you <i>really</i> want to \u201cMake new Exalta,\u201d what you really need is a lot of social influence dice, a pliable god, and a catastrophe. There\u2019s nothing stopping you from engineering an emergency worthy of the Exigence and then convincing a god to make an Exigent, and this is categorically similar to doing so via sorcerous working inasmuch as both methods involve equal parts rolling dice and convincing your ST to let you get away with your shenanigans.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This sounds like something a Sidereal would probably do","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T18:39:52-07:00","id":1323816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323711#post1323711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My operating theory for some time has been that Exalts really shouldn't be able to create more Exalts, <i>but</i>, they should be able to create something new that is to Exalts as Exalts are to gods or gods are to Primordials or Primordials are to... the... infinite roiling Wyld? So:<br /> <br /> Whatever it was in the Wyld that gave rise to the Primordials, if such things are meaningfully distinct -&gt; Primordials -&gt; Gods -&gt; Exalted -&gt; ????<br /> <br /> Because if the answer to the question &quot;What comes next in the cycle after Exalted?&quot; is &quot;More Exalted, possibly forever,&quot; that's boring.<br /> <br /> (And yes, I know there's arguably another version of this that goes Wyld -&gt; Primordials -&gt; elementals -&gt; Whatever the elementals could have gotten around to doing, if they had, which they don't appear to have done.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well in general yes I was wanting this to, but the setting has a troublesome conceit that seems to imply only Exalted are worth playing/capable of change/power. So I guess another type of Exalt. Basically rather then the Exalted of a great being, you become maybe the Exalted of a great power, say a Solar harnessing a Mindless power like a Shinma or Fate or Ideals or just teaming up with a power that lacks a human mindset to help harness it into an Exaltation.<br /> <br /> Also I wasn't thinking of these Exalts being servants, more I was implying with comments that they would help fill in for the Vacuum left by the Corruption of half the Solar Host as well as fill in areas that could use Exalted supervision like the Underworld or Alien corners.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T18:41:31-07:00","id":1323817,"title":"","content":"Also I figure this could be just a different origin for an Exalt that essentially could be created with the Exigent Mechanical advice. Because it's not like I have to adhere to canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T19:39:28-07:00","id":1323829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323816#post1323816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well in general yes I was wanting this to, but the setting has a troublesome conceit that seems to imply only Exalted are worth playing/capable of change/power.</div> </div> </div> </div>If anything it\u2019s a headcanon that\u2019s far wider-spread than was ever intended, considering that all three editions have had rules for play as mortals.<br /> <br /> (The idea also pretty blatantly ignores the existence of the Guild.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T22:07:57-07:00","id":1323858,"title":"","content":"It's notable too that it's not like the world having not all the Solars be Solars is some hole that needs fixed or &quot;flaw&quot; in the world. There was less than two-dozen for the last fifteen centuries, and the world carried on. A big thing to remember, especially in 3e context, is that Contagion-level existential threats are not something that we probably have to worry about again anytime soon. I twas a one-off event that probably has no past precedent or future potential equivilant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T22:22:46-07:00","id":1323863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323858#post1323858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's notable too that it's not like the world having not all the Solars be Solars is some hole that needs fixed or &quot;flaw&quot; in the world. There was less than two-dozen for the last fifteen centuries, and the world carried on. A big thing to remember, especially in 3e context, is that Contagion-level existential threats are not something that we probably have to worry about again anytime soon. I twas a one-off event that probably has no past precedent or future potential equivilant.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well a two off event that happened simultaneously as Balor and the Contagion two pronged the world. Also not being vigilant of such threats seemed to have been an error, if it wasn't for the fact the Solars were gone and everyone was arguing Creation wouldn't have been nearly wiped out. And the 1st age accounts we had lots of similar threats that were nipped in the bud because Exalted were running around all willy nilly smiting the apocalypse in the face or being dangers themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T02:21:10-07:00","id":1323892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323776#post1323776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Law of Diminishment, while I doubt we'll ever mention that by name in a book, I think it's an attempt to curb the Infinite Exalts issue</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, in its original reference, it's entirely concerned with why the Yozis would go for corrupting Solars rather than making their own, and since then its only visible manifestation has been as a source of tension for small gods dealing with the Exigence.<br /> <br /> And Vance has said it's going to be a consideration behind the Dark Mother, which I find to be the first truly intriguing reveal about her; what could her motives be that leave her willing to make that sacrifice?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why can't my Twilight make Orichalcum Castes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Surely Alchemicals' own mythology already covers that, with the necessary involvement of somebody mutated by Authochthon.<br /> <br /> An explanation for why Twilights can't replicate it seems as simple as reminders that the Alchemical Exalted are not robots.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also a Tolkien reference in a game deliberately devoid of them, which makes me think it's not a deliberate Tolkien reference: You <i>can</i> make something greater than yourself, but you forever diminish yourself in doing so. Sauron's creation of the Rings forever changes and diminishes him.</div> </div> </div> </div>To add to it probably not being a deliberate Tolkien reference, Tolkien didn't write that as an inherent property of forging Rings; Sauron needed to specifically add some oomph to the One to make it strong enough to enslave the others, and the only ingredient he had was himself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the Ring, and those it Chooses, comes great power, but without the Ring Sauron's but a shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, that was just how the movies played it. In the books, even without the Ring, Sauron is politically and mystically the most powerful being in Middle Earth. For all Gandalf's &quot;he needs this to cover the world in a second darkness&quot;, the council of Elrond went hard on emphasizing that the Ring was important because destroying it was their only means of stopping that from happening.<br /> <br /> One of Tolkien's letters had it that nobody besides Gandalf wielding the Ring would be capable of harnessing its power in a manner that would truly render Sauron subservient; in a military contest, he'd still have a good shot, and in a direct confrontation there would be no question.<br /> <br /> Tolkien certainly held that, if Gollum hadn't intervened and the Nazgul had caught up to Frodo, they wouldn't really be able to harm him anymore, and Sauron would have personally gone to get the Ring himself.<br /> <br /> Apologies for the digression, it's just one of my stronger interests.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T05:22:20-07:00","id":1323924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323892#post1323892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Apologies for the digression, it's just one of my stronger interests.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never apologize for Tolkien discussions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T09:38:37-07:00","id":1323973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323863#post1323863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well a two off event that happened simultaneously as Balor and the Contagion two pronged the world. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't know if they are not linked or not actually. For all we know, the Contagion allowed Balor to happen. The two events are usually talkeda bout as an Era with one-another as they kidn fo played on one-another. This is accounting that in 3e, we don't even know if they are separate or why they happened.<br /> <br /> But again, no event like them seems to have ever happened in all of the history of the Age of Man. Most of Creation's issues during hte First Age were things of human cause or origin from what I remember with the timeline. This does include shit like necromancer kings, and there are things like behemoths, demons, and monsters, sure. But a lot of the Ages seem defined by human (ie Exalted/necromancer/whatever) causes. It's still likely that such a thing never happened before, and never will happen again. Especially in 3e and its emphasis on non-existential threats justifying Exalted presence a priori in some things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323863#post1323863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Also not being vigilant of such threats seemed to have been an error, if it wasn't for the fact the Solars were gone and everyone was arguing Creation wouldn't have been nearly wiped out. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't actually know this. For all we know, the Solars were probably just as likely to have something worse in the interum seven or so centuries before the Contagion hit. Or would have <span style=\"color:#DCDDDE\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">exacerbated </span></span></span>it. Or that since there's only a few hundred of them and Creation is huge they can't be everywhere at once and things happened so fast that we would have lost fewer total people, but still lost some large fraction of Creation's population.<br /> <br /> And again, since it'll likely never happen agin, thinkgint hat you need to invest in some Secretary Chosen to fill in for you to fix such a hypothetical thing is basically worrying about needing a Bear Patrol and anti-Tiger Rocks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323863#post1323863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... And the 1st age accounts we had lots of similar threats that were nipped in the bud because Exalted were running around all willy nilly smiting the apocalypse in the face or being dangers themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding of things from what we saw of the First Age so far is that nine times out of ten it was probably an Exalt or group of Exalts causing problems, and that it's also not clear anytyhing ever on the scale of the Contagion in scope and total destruction was around. Things might have gotten werid or upheaved, but I doubt there was as much existential as Balor's crack at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":353,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","user":"Blaque","date":". 07-12-2019, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T09:55:59-07:00","id":1323980,"title":"","content":"Just as a reminder, even one of the most apocalyptic beasties to rampage around in the First Age and introduced in Ex3, Karvara was unleashed <i>by a traitorous Solar</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T10:17:36-07:00","id":1323992,"title":"","content":"It should be mentioned that there were a couple of huge threats the Exalted had to fight; the Scorpion Empire and the Niobaran League (the Niobaran League admittedly did include some humans, but also a lot of non-humans, and the Voice in the Trench was I'm sure inhuman).<br /> <br /> But I'd agree with Blaque that 9 times out of 10, the most dangerous violence was from different Exalts; the Sun-and-Moon war, the Sunstrife Wars, and eventually the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> I certainly get the impression that the Great Contagion was the biggest disaster that happened in Creation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For all we know, the Contagion allowed Balor to happen. </div> </div> </div>My impression was always that the Balorian Crusade happened when it did because the Raksha saw the Great Contagion had weakened Creation's defences.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T11:15:14-07:00","id":1324008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1323992#post1323992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My impression was always that the Balorian Crusade happened when it did because the Raksha saw the Great Contagion had weakened Creation's defences.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the First and Forsaken Lion inviting them in to play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T11:45:34-07:00","id":1324018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uknown DarkLord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1324008#post1324008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And the First and Forsaken Lion inviting them in to play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like literally stated as a fact he sent them an invitation and that is why they were free to assault in waves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T15:23:13-07:00","id":1324054,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s a 2e retcon, and is not necessarily in play in 3e.<br /> <br /> Edit: or, wait, was that the 2e retcon, or was the retcon that the Fair Folk coming in was what cured the Contagion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T16:22:23-07:00","id":1324066,"title":"","content":"I think the cure?<br /> <br /> I believe it was 1st ed that said he might have invited them. I think 2nd ed took out that he (might have?) invited them because he was plotting to overthrow the Deathlords, and instead put it down to incompetence.<br /> <br /> I'll have to check later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T16:57:49-07:00","id":1324075,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure that even if he invited them in, it may not have done anything to cure or mess up the damage from the Contagion. 1e implied at times there were segments of the population just outright immune to it (basically diseases are never 100% contagious). The Fair Folk were meant to be the coup de grace in 1e to my understanding.<br /> <br /> None of this is relevant in 3e mind, where we know neither the canoncial source of the Contagion or the reasoning (or even existence) of Balor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T19:59:27-07:00","id":1324117,"title":"","content":"You know, I'm entirely on board with the idea that the Fair Folk were not so hobbled that they needed Exalted permission to invade the world like that, but I will always be a bit enamoured of that line &quot;do as you wish with the living, for our concern is with the dead&quot;, or whatever words to that effect.<br /> <br /> Anyway, to get back on track, I find the reasoning of &quot;the Exalted have to make more Exalted, because only Exalted accomplish things&quot; to be very circular. Even if it was an accurate assessment, how is something that has not yet been created supposed to accomplish something?<br /> <br /> &quot;Let us make men our champions, and bestow our power upon them.&quot;<br /> &quot;But Suuuuuuun, only gods have ever accomplished anything!&quot;<br /> &quot;Jesus Christ, let my unprecedented creation at least have a chance to strut its stuff, you incessant whingers.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T22:50:57-07:00","id":1324360,"title":"","content":"Preamble: I may be a bit late to the party. However, I believe the best counterargument to a null set declaration is an example. So, in an effort to provide a thought-provoking, workable set of sub-Exalts, I present the below. More as a setup for their own chronicle, or to appear as allies or antagonists, than as something to incorporate in an existing Solar campaign as the work of a player. <br /> <br /> The Exalted of Balthazar, he of the Eclipse Caste, Grandchildren of the Unconquered Sun, Prisms of Light<br /> <br /> Born in the time of strife that epitomized the Second Age of Man, Balthazar was graced by the Unconquered Sun, found others of his kind, braved the Wyld Hunt, and wrested the Creation Ruling Mandate back from the Scarlet Dynasty and their Sidereal enablers to establish the Third Age of Man, as glorious as the first. During this epic journey, he was deeply influenced by a god, not the absent Unconquered Sun, rather Hiroko, the god of inter-Exalt relations. Hiroko was a valued and respected god in the First Age where he promoted harmony among the various stripes of Exalted. Listened to and respected by the Solar Deliberative, the Silver Pact, the Five-Score Fellowship and the Dragon-Blooded host alike, he had a divine nature that allowed an empathetic understanding so total he could forget his own prior thoughts on an issue. That is, until the Great Prophecy was cast. Hiroko was one of the first gods targeted in the Sidereal political offensive leading up to the Usurpation. The embittered god languished in the slums of Yu-Shan for fifteen centuries before hope returned to him with the rebirth of the Solars, an in particular his meeting with the Eclipse Caste Balthazar. <br /> <br /> Balthazar saw the good of negotiation, of empathy, of reason and of mutual self-interest. But, to empathize with all is not to become them. The sun shines so brightly that it cannot see from the darkness that inhibits others' souls. Even the Night Caste carries their spark into the void, to shine forth again when justice calls. Balthazar took Hiroko's lessons to heart, especially after the god's soul was torn asunder by the Wyld's corruption in the Breach of Swar under the Divine General Supreme, Aidenweiss' second reign. <br /> <br /> So, Balthazar set out to create what he strove to be - to cleave his own nature from his Exalted patron and imbue it in his children of the spirit through the method of Exaltation itself. A grand tale in its own right those trials would be, though they are not the subject at hand. The results of his labor are the Exalted of Balthazar, colloquially known as the Prisms, of which there are only seven. Scholars speculate that the Prisms are themselves the hybrids of the Exalted of the Unconquered Sun and the never-realized Exalted of Hiroko, though no provable experiment has been proposed to affirm or discredit the speculation.<br /> <br /> During an eclipse, a Prism may clasp two beings and produce a perfect understanding between them. All of their internal lives, their past and hoped-for future, their viewpoints and heartfelt principles, are completely transparent to the two so connected via the Prism and the Prism herself. The Prism who accomplishes this connection is forever changed, burning away any Aspect she may have coursing through her and replacing it with two new shafts of light. She becomes uncannily like what the progeny of the two would have been, had she been born of their issue twenty years prior. <br /> <br /> If she makes peace between two warring tribes of humanity, she becomes human, with only the latent power to change again at the next eclipse. Her features are a blend of the two tribes, and she is often granted an accentless bilingual tongue. She remembers her past lives, her past identities. She knows her previous skills, but should she, say, speak what was once her native tongue, now it will issue forth with an accent from one or both of her newly adopted tribes. When the beings she grants understanding to are different than humanity, she blends their natures as well. Should she make an accord between warring gods and elementals, she will be both divine, sharing in the touched god's nature, and also have powers over Creation's elements. Her human nature is forgotten, though the latent power of the Prism remains.<br /> <br /> Prisms have no known natural lifespan, since so many effectively regain their youth each eclipse. Each knows the exact date and time of the next such celestial event, and manages to stave off a natural death until that time even if neither of their progenitor beings could possibly live that long. Should one perish, their soul makes its way to Lytek's care, and finds another host among humanity who desires to know the other as completely as the self - for good or ill. Their moment of Exaltation replaces this yearning with a transformation into the last hybrid form that Prism's soul achieved. <br /> <br /> By this time in the Late Third Age, only a few in Yu-Shan know where the Prisms might be or what natures they currently take. Look for them in times of great strife where understanding might save countless lives, or where two beings of great power can be coerced into meeting under an eclipse for selfish ends. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T03:15:48-07:00","id":1324394,"title":"","content":"See that is interesting and I don't mind such beings. I especially like the concept of Hiroko, and I wouldn't of conceived of beings like these.<br /> <br /> So lets say I don't use the Term Exalted, So I make beings like a Keyblade Wielder, Beings whose blood become primordial Symbiotes, Guyver Style Alchemicals, Stand Users, and beings with Cursed Brands which give them power along with dire consequences. Say I don't call these beings Exalted but they are comparable to Exalted. Will that be more of an issue for people then calling them Exalted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T03:43:25-07:00","id":1324402,"title":"","content":"I suspect so.<br /> <br /> &quot;Exalted&quot; implies that a)they're as powerful as PCs, b)derive their powers from the themes of their creator, and c)can replicate all over the setting.<br /> <br /> As I mentioned, you can create all sorts of weird stuff with sorcery, etc. Creating powerful servants isn't really the issue, it's the above.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T04:36:18-07:00","id":1324412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1324402#post1324402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect so.<br /> <br /> &quot;Exalted&quot; implies that a)they're as powerful as PCs, b)derive their powers from the themes of their creator, and c)can replicate all over the setting.<br /> <br /> As I mentioned, you can create all sorts of weird stuff with sorcery, etc. Creating powerful servants isn't really the issue, it's the above.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's the point making them as powerful as PCs, or at least circumstantially approaching. And not something simple like a dude with one trick. Though Technically with Sorcery you can make spirits stronger then a lot of Dragonblooded, I'd wager on Octavian over most Dragonblooded in a cage fight.<br /> I'm <br /> I mean beings with their own charm trees. Maybe not as robust as Exalted ones but ample enough where you could create a group of them without being redundant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T18:01:13-07:00","id":1324590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1324412#post1324412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well that's the point making them as powerful as PCs, or at least circumstantially approaching. And not something simple like a dude with one trick. Though Technically with Sorcery you can make spirits stronger then a lot of Dragonblooded, I'd wager on Octavian over most Dragonblooded in a cage fight.<br /> I'm<br /> I mean beings with their own charm trees. Maybe not as robust as Exalted ones but ample enough where you could create a group of them without being redundant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems by then they stop being PC's and are a part of the next game session's background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T22:13:23-07:00","id":1326886,"title":"","content":"So I theorize at least one of the new Exalted are Chosen/Foresaken of the Great Curse, I'm guessing the Soul Bitten. Been thinking about this more as I play Darksouls and I feel being Chosen of the Great Curse would be a suitable source of Exaltation, the power being the Curse. If I make my own version of such beings another entity could just be vehicle for the Curse.<br /> <br /> And how free are we in the power levels of non Exalted Potent Beings like the Dragon Kings and Mountainfolk, theoretically weaker then Dragonblooded but still potent I imagine. This makes me hope we get Changelings, not just Godblooded aspected to Raksha but Mortals taken as babes to Rakshastan and who evolve into Fae beings. I see World of Darkness splats as good inspiration for nonExalted Supernatural beings. So perhaps they have powersets or even charms, but unlike the Exalted their charms aren't balanced to cover all angles, like how Exalted in general have Integrity Protection Charms and some form of Area of Effect avoidance.<br /> <br /> But other Examples possibly Patronless Exalted besides Foresaken of the Great Curse, are the Chosen Undead/Unkindled, the Chosen of the Keyblade, Maybe even Chosen of the Directions (basically this would be an artificial Created Elemental Exalted Not Chosen of the Dragons but of Creation Itself, the Chosen of Oblivion (we already god Abyssal), and the Chosen of Apocalypse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T22:37:20-07:00","id":1326890,"title":"","content":"Considering the devs' statements about the Dream-Souled, I don't see the Great Curse being their patron. &gt;.&gt;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T22:40:10-07:00","id":1326891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1326886#post1326886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I theorize at least one of the new Exalted are Chosen/Foresaken of the Great Curse, I'm guessing the Soul Bitten. Been thinking about this more as I play Darksouls and I feel being Chosen of the Great Curse would be a suitable source of Exaltation, the power being the Curse. If I make my own version of such beings another entity could just be vehicle for the Curse.<br /> <br /> And how free are we in the power levels of non Exalted Potent Beings like the Dragon Kings and Mountainfolk, theoretically weaker then Dragonblooded but still potent I imagine. This makes me hope we get Changelings, not just Godblooded aspected to Raksha but Mortals taken as babes to Rakshastan and who evolve into Fae beings. I see World of Darkness splats as good inspiration for nonExalted Supernatural beings. So perhaps they have powersets or even charms, but unlike the Exalted their charms aren't balanced to cover all angles, like how Exalted in general have Integrity Protection Charms and some form of Area of Effect avoidance.<br /> <br /> But other Examples possibly Patronless Exalted besides Foresaken of the Great Curse, are the Chosen Undead/Unkindled, the Chosen of the Keyblade, Maybe even Chosen of the Directions (basically this would be an artificial Created Elemental Exalted Not Chosen of the Dragons but of Creation Itself, the Chosen of Oblivion (we already god Abyssal), and the Chosen of Apocalypse.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Changeling sounds like Myst, so they exist in some faction.<br /> Chosen of the Keyblade sounds like &quot;Artifact passed down Exigence&quot;. I don't know enough about KH to pick the god who died for that.<br /> Chosen Undead as in dark soul's &quot;just won't die&quot; sounds like liminals &quot;I only die if beheaded or drowned&quot;. <br /> What would thte powers of a Chosen of the Great Curse be like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T22:49:55-07:00","id":1326893,"title":"","content":"Well I would imagine the power of Cursing, Vengeance, Revenge, Secrecy, Fate, and being Kryptonite to Exalted that took part in the War, maybe even the Gods as well. So the Abyssals would be a Scythe to reap all of Creation, the Foresaken of the Great would be like blades destined for the Sheath that would be the Exalted and the Incarnae. Assassin's to the Abyssals butchers. Oblivion's version of Sidereals maybe be a good analogy but they wouldn't be like Sidereals or Getimians.<br /> <br /> But you can imagine the evocative nature of Curses to Boil your blood and wrack your body till the last pulse. To turn your shadows to flames and breath to ash. It could go in a number of Directions, maybe even a few Castes.<br /> <br /> The thing with making custom headcanon Homebrew Exalts is you aren't compelled to make 100+ of them you could just make a handful, even if you have a potent source of power capable of making even more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T02:47:39-07:00","id":1326920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1323141-what-is-stopping-your-circle-from-creating-their-own-exalts?p=1326886#post1326886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Been thinking about this more as I play Darksouls and I feel being Chosen of the Great Curse would be a suitable source of Exaltation, the power being the Curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren't the Neverborn still the cause of the Great Curse?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T03